  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Core runtime",
      "items": [
        "The repo exposes a Typer CLI and a FastAPI server as the runtime entry points; the tool-calling agent loop is the main investigative path.",
        "Toolsets are plugin-based and can query Kubernetes, Prometheus, Grafana, cloud APIs, SQL, and MCP services.",
        "The same runtime supports local CLI use and background operator mode in production.",
        "Exact cluster topology is not declared in the repo; this area is intentionally marked as unknown."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Cross-boundary mechanisms",
      "items": [
        "HTTPS / webhook / API from existing alerting and ticketing systems into the runtime.",
        "HTTPS API calls to LLM providers and platform services such as Supabase / Ephaptic.",
        "OTLP and telemetry exports to observability vendors, with Sentry and Braintrust explicitly present in dependency and runtime code.",
        "OAuth and environment-based configuration are local trust-plane inputs; the repo does not declare a single identity broker."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Ownership and trust",
      "items": [
        "The public side is untrusted input; the private runtime boundary is the operational trust domain.",
        "Platform-managed state sits in Supabase-backed service layers, while the customer controls local config and credentials.",
        "The repo names external dependencies but not a concrete production provider, region, or network mapping; that is deliberately left unknown."
      ]
    }
